-- The schema Domix starts from: every table, index, trigger and the 283-row product template
-- catalogue, as the migrations before the first deploy left them. They were collapsed into this one
-- while no database but a developer's existed to migrate.
--
-- **Generated by pg_dump, not written by hand.** Edit the database, not this file: add a new
-- migration beside it. Re-collapsing is only ever right again if production is rebuilt from zero.
--
-- **Two things pg_dump emits are stripped on the way in, and re-adding them breaks a real deploy:**
-- psql's \restrict meta-commands, which golang-migrate sends to the server as SQL; and
-- COMMENT ON EXTENSION, which only an extension's owner may run - postgis is untrusted, so in
-- production a superuser creates both extensions before the api's own role gets here.

-- under the C locale lower() leaves Cyrillic alone, so "цемент" would stop finding "Цемент" with
-- nothing to report it. refused here rather than in production, where the first owner to search
-- their own catalogue would be the one to find out.
DO $$
BEGIN
    IF lower('ЦЁ') <> 'цё' THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION 'this database does not lowercase Cyrillic, so product search would be case-sensitive - recreate it with a UTF-8 locale such as en_US.UTF-8';
    END IF;
END $$;

